# Line endings are load-bearing in this repo, so they are pinned rather than
# left to each clone's core.autocrlf.
#
# A shell script checked out with CRLF fails on Linux with
#   bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M
# which would break the POSIX launcher for anyone cloning on Windows and
# running on Linux (or through WSL). Python is pinned to LF for the same
# reason - a CRLF shebang line breaks `./collect-image-inventory.py`.
#
# The .bat files are the opposite case: cmd.exe is happiest with CRLF, and
# the launchers are shipped ASCII+CRLF deliberately.

*           text=auto eol=lf

*.sh        text eol=lf
*.py        text eol=lf
*.md        text eol=lf
*.txt       text eol=lf
.gitignore  text eol=lf

*.bat       text eol=crlf

# Never normalise binary-ish things if any are added later.
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.webp      binary
*.jsonl     binary
